  "notes": [
   "The circuit image shows two 2-lead force-sensing resistors; they are mapped to the matched parts (potentiometer-10k and photoresistor). The potentiometer is used as a variable resistor: only SIG and VCC are connected, GND is left unconnected.",
   "Breadboard hole names were mapped from the image onto the catalogue naming: the image's top half (rows j-f) is bank 't' (rows a-e, j->a ... f->e) and the lower half (rows e-a) is bank 'b' (rows f-j, e->f ... a->j). Exact columns are estimated from the picture.",
   "Top rails: tp = + (red line), tn = - (black). Bottom rails: bp = +, bn = -. Long wires link top and bottom rails.",
   "The pushbutton straddles the centre gap: side 1 (column 5) is on 5V, side 2 (column 7) goes to Arduino pin 2 and to the 10K pull-down resistor to GND, matching the schematic.",
   "Sensor 1 (potentiometer) junction goes to A1 with a 10K resistor to GND; sensor 2 (photoresistor) junction goes to A0 with a 10K resistor to GND, as drawn in the image.",
   "The sensors' leads plug directly into the breadboard, as drawn."
  ]
 },
